  "files": [
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Pixel Calculator</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"card\" aria-labelledby=\"title\">\n  <h1 id=\"title\">Pixel Calc</h1>\n  <div class=\"field\">\n    <label for=\"left\">Left number</label>\n    <input id=\"left\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"e.g. -12.5\">\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"field\">\n    <label for=\"operation\">Operation</label>\n    <select id=\"operation\">\n      <option value=\"add\">Add (+)</option>\n      <option value=\"subtract\">Subtract (−)</option>\n      <option value=\"multiply\">Multiply (×)</option>\n      <option value=\"divide\">Divide (÷)</option>\n    </select>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"field\">\n    <label for=\"right\">Right number</label>\n    <input id=\"right\" type=\"text\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"e.g. 3\">\n  </div>\n  <button id=\"calculate\" type=\"button\">Calculate</button>\n  <div class=\"field\">\n    <label for=\"result\">Result</label>\n    <output id=\"result\" for=\"left right operation\" aria-live=\"polite\">0</output>\n  </div>\n</main>\n<script src=\"app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
      "description": "Main HTML with labeled inputs, operation select, calculate button, and result output."
    },
    {
      "path": "styles.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1b1035;\n  --panel: #2e1f5e;\n  --accent: #ffd23f;\n  --text: #f4f0ff;\n  --muted: #b9a9e8;\n}\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  padding: 24px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, #251548 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, #251548 25%, transparent 25%),\n    linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 75%, #251548 75%),\n    linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 75%, #251548 75%);\n  background-size: 32px 32px;\n  background-position: 0 0, 0 16px, 16px -16px, -16px 0;\n  font-family: \"Courier New\", ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  color: var(--text);\n}\n.card {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 380px;\n  background: var(--panel);\n  padding: 28px 24px;\n  border: 4px solid var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 #00000066;\n}\nh1 {\n  margin: 0 0 20px;\n  font-size: 26px;\n  letter-spacing: 2px;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  text-align: center;\n}\n.field { margin-bottom: 16px; }\nlabel {\n  display: block;\n  margin-bottom: 6px;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\ninput, select, output {\n  width: 100%;\n  display: block;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  padding: 10px 12px;\n  color: var(--text);\n  background: #1b1035;\n  border: 3px solid var(--muted);\n  border-radius: 0;\n}\ninput:focus, select:focus, button:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\noutput {\n  min-height: 46px;\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n  color: var(--accent);\n  font-weight: bold;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n}\nbutton {\n  width: 100%;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  padding: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  color: #1b1035;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  border: 3px solid var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #00000088;\n  transition: transform 0.05s ease;\n}\nbutton:hover { background: #ffe27a; }\nbutton:active {\n  transform: translate(3px, 3px);\n  box-shadow: 1px 1px 0 #00000088;\n}\n",
      "description": "Pixel-art themed CSS with cohesive palette, centered card, focus/hover/pressed states, responsive to 360px."
    },
    {
      "path": "app.js",
      "content": "(function () {\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  var leftEl = document.getElementById(\"left\");\n  var rightEl = document.getElementById(\"right\");\n  var opEl = document.getElementById(\"operation\");\n  var btn = document.getElementById(\"calculate\");\n  var resultEl = document.getElementById(\"result\");\n\n  function parseNumber(raw) {\n    if (raw === null || raw === undefined) return NaN;\n    var trimmed = String(raw).trim();\n    if (trimmed === \"\") return NaN;\n    var n = Number(trimmed);\n    return isFinite(n) ? n : NaN;\n  }\n\n  function compute(a, b, op) {\n    switch (op) {\n      case \"add\": return a + b;\n      case \"subtract\": return a - b;\n      case \"multiply\": return a * b;\n      case \"divide\": return b === 0 ? NaN : a / b;\n      default: return NaN;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function calculate() {\n    var a = parseNumber(leftEl.value);\n    var b = parseNumber(rightEl.value);\n    var op = opEl.value;\n\n    if (isNaN(a) || isNaN(b)) {\n      resultEl.textContent = \"Error\";\n      return;\n    }\n\n    var out = compute(a, b, op);\n    if (!isFinite(out)) {\n      resultEl.textContent = \"Error\";\n      return;\n    }\n\n    resultEl.textContent = String(out);\n  }\n\n  btn.addEventListener(\"click\", calculate);\n\n  [leftEl, rightEl].forEach(function (el) {\n    el.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) {\n      if (e.key === \"Enter\") {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        calculate();\n      }\n    });\n  });\n})();\n",
      "description": "Calculator logic: validates finite numbers, handles division by zero, supports negatives, outputs numeric result or Error."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Calculator\n\nAn offline pixel-style calculator that combines two numbers with a chosen operation.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser (no server or install needed).\n2. Enter a **Left number** and a **Right number** (negative values allowed).\n3. Pick an **Operation**: Add, Subtract, Multiply, or Divide.\n4. Press **Calculate** (or press Enter in either number field).\n5. The **Result** field shows only the numeric result, or `Error`.\n\n## Error handling\n\n`Error` is shown when:\n\n- Either input is empty or not a finite number.\n- The operation is division and the right number is `0`.\n- The computed result is not finite (e.g. overflow).\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- Every control has an associated `<label>`.\n- All controls are keyboard accessible with visible focus outlines.\n- The result region uses `aria-live=\"polite\"` so screen readers announce updates.\n\n## Tech\n\nPlain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No packages, storage, network requests, or external assets. Files: `index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`.\n",
      "description": "README with usage instructions, error handling, accessibility notes, and tech summary."
    }
  ]
